\hypertarget{database-implementation}{%
\subsection{5. DATABASE IMPLEMENTATION}\label{database-implementation}}

\hypertarget{mongodb-connection}{%
\subsubsection{5.1 MongoDB Connection}\label{mongodb-connection}}

\textbf{Location}: server/server.js \textbf{Connection String}:
mongodb://localhost:27017/nestup\_bd \textbf{ODM}: Mongoose for schema
definition and data modeling

\textbf{Connection Process}: 1. Load MongoDB URI from environment
variables 2. Use mongoose.connect() with connection options 3. Handle
connection events (connected, error, disconnected) 4. Implement graceful
shutdown on process termination

\hypertarget{database-schema-design}{%
\subsubsection{5.2 Database Schema
Design}\label{database-schema-design}}

\hypertarget{collections-overview}{%
\paragraph{5.2.1 Collections Overview}\label{collections-overview}}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  \textbf{users}: User accounts and profiles
\item
  \textbf{services}: Property listings and details
\item
  \textbf{bookings}: Booking requests and status
\item
  \textbf{payments}: Payment transactions and history
\end{itemize}

\hypertarget{relationships}{%
\paragraph{5.2.2 Relationships}\label{relationships}}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  User → Services (One-to-Many): User can own multiple properties
\item
  Service → Bookings (One-to-Many): Property can have multiple bookings
\item
  User → Bookings (One-to-Many): User can make multiple bookings
\item
  Booking → Payment (One-to-One): Each booking has one payment
\item
  User → Payments (One-to-Many): User can have multiple payments
\end{itemize}

\hypertarget{indexes}{%
\paragraph{5.2.3 Indexes}\label{indexes}}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  Users: email (unique), createdAt
\item
  Services: location.district, location.area, price, createdAt
\item
  Bookings: user, service, startDate, endDate
\item
  Payments: user, booking, status, createdAt
\end{itemize}

\hypertarget{data-validation}{%
\subsubsection{5.3 Data Validation}\label{data-validation}}

\textbf{Schema-Level Validation}: - Required fields enforcement - Data
type validation - Enum value restrictions - String length limits -
Number range validation - Email format validation

\textbf{Application-Level Validation}: - Business logic validation -
Cross-field validation - Custom validation functions - Error message
customization

================================================================================

\hypertarget{api-endpoints-and-data-flow}{%
\subsection{6. API ENDPOINTS AND DATA
FLOW}\label{api-endpoints-and-data-flow}}

\hypertarget{authentication-flow}{%
\subsubsection{6.1 Authentication Flow}\label{authentication-flow}}

\textbf{Registration Process}: 1. Frontend: User submits registration
form 2. Frontend: POST /api/auth/register with user data 3. Backend:
Validate input data 4. Backend: Hash password using bcrypt 5. Backend:
Create user in database 6. Backend: Generate JWT token 7. Backend: Set
HTTP-only cookie with token 8. Backend: Return user data (excluding
password) 9. Frontend: Update AuthContext with user data 10. Frontend:
Redirect to dashboard

\textbf{Login Process}: 1. Frontend: User submits login form 2.
Frontend: POST /api/auth/login with credentials 3. Backend: Find user by
email 4. Backend: Compare password with stored hash 5. Backend: Generate
JWT token if valid 6. Backend: Set HTTP-only cookie with token 7.
Backend: Return user data 8. Frontend: Update AuthContext 9. Frontend:
Redirect to intended page

\hypertarget{service-management-flow}{%
\subsubsection{6.2 Service Management
Flow}\label{service-management-flow}}

\textbf{Service Creation}: 1. Frontend: User fills ProvideService form
2. Frontend: Upload images via FormData 3. Frontend: POST /api/services
with service data 4. Backend: Validate user authentication 5. Backend:
Process uploaded images 6. Backend: Create service in database 7.
Backend: Return created service data 8. Frontend: Show success message
and redirect

\textbf{Service Search}: 1. Frontend: User applies filters on Search
page 2. Frontend: GET /api/services with query parameters 3. Backend:
Build MongoDB filter object 4. Backend: Execute paginated query with
population 5. Backend: Return services array with pagination info 6.
Frontend: Transform data for display 7. Frontend: Render ListingCard
components

\hypertarget{booking-and-payment-flow}{%
\subsubsection{6.3 Booking and Payment
Flow}\label{booking-and-payment-flow}}

\textbf{Complete Booking Process}: 1. Frontend: User clicks ``Book'' on
ListingCard 2. Frontend: Navigate to Payment page with property data 3.
Frontend: User completes payment form steps 4. Frontend: POST
/api/bookings to create booking 5. Backend: Validate service exists and
availability 6. Backend: Check for booking conflicts 7. Backend:
Calculate total amount and fees 8. Backend: Create booking with
`pending' status 9. Backend: Return booking data with ID 10. Frontend:
POST /api/payments with booking ID 11. Backend: Validate payment details
12. Backend: Create payment record 13. Backend: Update booking payment
status 14. Backend: Return payment confirmation 15. Frontend: Show
success message 16. Frontend: Navigate to dashboard

\hypertarget{wishlist-management}{%
\subsubsection{6.4 Wishlist Management}\label{wishlist-management}}

\textbf{Add to Wishlist}: 1. Frontend: User clicks ``Save'' on
ListingCard 2. Frontend: POST /api/wishlist/add with serviceId 3.
Backend: Validate authentication and service 4. Backend: Check if
already in wishlist 5. Backend: Add to user's wishlist array 6. Backend:
Return success response 7. Frontend: Update UI state

================================================================================

\hypertarget{authentication-system}{%
\subsection{7. AUTHENTICATION SYSTEM}\label{authentication-system}}

\hypertarget{jwt-implementation}{%
\subsubsection{7.1 JWT Implementation}\label{jwt-implementation}}

\textbf{Token Generation}: - Payload: \{ userId, email, iat, exp \} -
Secret: Stored in environment variables - Expiration: 7 days - Storage:
HTTP-only cookies for security

\textbf{Token Verification}: - Middleware: verifyToken() function -
Extraction: From cookies or Authorization header - Validation: JWT
signature and expiration - User Lookup: Find user by decoded ID -
Request Attachment: Add user object to req.user

\hypertarget{password-security}{%
\subsubsection{7.2 Password Security}\label{password-security}}

\textbf{Hashing}: - Algorithm: bcrypt with salt rounds (10) - Timing:
Pre-save middleware in User model - Comparison: comparePassword() method
- Storage: Never store plain text passwords

\hypertarget{route-protection}{%
\subsubsection{7.3 Route Protection}\label{route-protection}}

\textbf{Protected Routes}: - All routes requiring authentication use
verifyToken middleware - Additional checkAuth middleware ensures user
exists - Role-based access control for admin functions - Owner-only
access for service management

================================================================================

\hypertarget{payment-system}{%
\subsection{8. PAYMENT SYSTEM}\label{payment-system}}

\hypertarget{payment-methods}{%
\subsubsection{8.1 Payment Methods}\label{payment-methods}}

\textbf{Supported Methods}: - Mobile Banking (bKash, Nagad, Rocket) -
Bank Transfer - Credit/Debit Card - Cash Payment

\textbf{Method-Specific Data}: - Mobile Banking: Phone number,
transaction ID - Bank Transfer: Bank name, account number - Credit Card:
Card number, expiry, CVV, holder name - Cash: Contact information for
arrangement

\hypertarget{payment-processing}{%
\subsubsection{8.2 Payment Processing}\label{payment-processing}}

\textbf{Payment States}: - pending: Initial state after creation -
processing: Payment being processed - completed: Payment successful -
failed: Payment failed with reason - refunded: Payment refunded -
cancelled: Payment cancelled by user

\textbf{Processing Flow}: 1. Create booking first 2. Validate payment
details 3. Create payment record 4. Process payment (simulated) 5.
Update payment status 6. Update booking payment status 7. Send
confirmation

\hypertarget{payment-history}{%
\subsubsection{8.3 Payment History}\label{payment-history}}

\textbf{Data Tracking}: - All payment transactions stored - Status
change history - Payment method details - Associated booking information
- Refund tracking

\textbf{Dashboard Integration}: - Payment history view in dashboard -
Filtering by status and date - Detailed payment information -
Download/export capabilities

================================================================================

