\hypertarget{frontend-backend-connection-flow}{%
\subsection{10. FRONTEND-BACKEND CONNECTION
FLOW}\label{frontend-backend-connection-flow}}

\hypertarget{api-communication-pattern}{%
\subsubsection{10.1 API Communication
Pattern}\label{api-communication-pattern}}

\textbf{Standard Request Flow}: 1. Frontend component initiates action
(user interaction) 2. Component calls fetch() with appropriate endpoint
3. Request includes authentication cookies automatically 4. Backend
middleware verifies authentication 5. Route handler processes request 6.
Database operations performed if needed 7. Response sent back to
frontend 8. Frontend updates UI based on response

\hypertarget{authentication-integration}{%
\subsubsection{10.2 Authentication
Integration}\label{authentication-integration}}

\textbf{Cookie-Based Authentication}: - JWT tokens stored in HTTP-only
cookies - Automatic inclusion in all requests - No manual token
management in frontend - Secure against XSS attacks

\textbf{AuthContext Integration}: - Global authentication state -
Automatic login status checking - Protected route handling - User data
availability across components

\hypertarget{error-handling}{%
\subsubsection{10.3 Error Handling}\label{error-handling}}

\textbf{Frontend Error Handling}: - Try-catch blocks around API calls -
User-friendly error messages - Loading state management - Fallback UI
for errors

\textbf{Backend Error Handling}: - Consistent error response format -
HTTP status codes - Detailed error messages - Logging for debugging

\hypertarget{data-transformation}{%
\subsubsection{10.4 Data Transformation}\label{data-transformation}}

\textbf{Backend to Frontend}: - MongoDB ObjectId to string conversion -
Date formatting - Price formatting - Image URL construction

\textbf{Frontend to Backend}: - Form data serialization - Date object
conversion - File upload handling - Validation before sending

================================================================================

